# Layout, set, declared family, lost: not every order climbs that alike. Five members meet at a parameter, which climbs to their family, and a stranger comes later: the whole family is lost, and every member that
# may be known by it joins. The stranger in the same step: each was lost by itself, nobody told the family, and the sixth member kept its proof. Which of the two a large program got hung on the clock.
# The nearest declared family of two layouts that stand in one lost family is lost, so both programs below end alike, in every order of the worklist.
#   abstract class Shape { }  Circle, Square, Triangle, Oval, Kite, Star extend Shape  Point     abstract class Tool { }  Hammer, Saw, Drill, File, Plane, Chisel extend Tool  Nail
#   function area(o) { return 1 }  function put(e) { e.x = null }  function same(v) { return v }  function use(o) { return 1 }  function lay(e) { e.x = null }
#   area(circle); area(triangle); area(oval); area(kite); area(star);  put(circle); put(square); put(oval); put(kite); put(star); put(same(same(point)));       the stranger has the longer way
#   use(hammer); use(drill); use(file); use(plane); use(chisel);  lay(hammer); lay(saw); lay(file); lay(plane); lay(chisel); lay(nail);                         the stranger comes with the five
# Triangle and Drill may be known by their families because five members meet at `area` and at `use`: up to four are a set, which names its members and no family.
# Without the rule the field of Drill is proven a string here, and that of Triangle null|string.
# RUN: link fields mechanisms=all
# CHECK: field L3.0 "x" proven=null|string
# CHECK: field L8.0 "x" proven=null|string
# RUN(OLDEST): link fields oldest-first mechanisms=all
# OLDEST: field L3.0 "x" proven=null|string
# OLDEST: field L8.0 "x" proven=null|string
# RUN(SCATTERED): link fields scattered mechanisms=all
# SCATTERED: field L3.0 "x" proven=null|string
# SCATTERED: field L8.0 "x" proven=null|string
# RUN(LOST): link functions mechanisms=all
# LOST: function f1 callers-known one-callee
# LOST-NEXT: parameter 0 {{*}}proven=L1|L2|L3|L10|L11|L12
# LOST: function f2 callers-known one-callee
# LOST-NEXT: parameter 0 {{*}}proven=L1|L2|L3|L4|L10|L11|L12
# LOST: function f4 callers-known one-callee
# LOST-NEXT: parameter 0 {{*}}proven=L6|L7|L8|L13|L14|L15
# LOST: function f5 callers-known one-callee
# LOST-NEXT: parameter 0 {{*}}proven=L6|L7|L8|L9|L13|L14|L15

